ply`, writes nothing.\n\n## Head\n\n62bd768af874fb3750eff21b2fd49e3dad31dec1\n\n## Summary\n\n`tools/audit/seat/prune_refs.py` encodes the brief's four rules and its four hazards as code:\n\n- keep `main`, and any ref whose pull request is OPEN (deleting that head closes the pull request);\n- delete a ref already merged into main (decision 0010 keeps its commits as the merge's second parent), and an unmerged `handoff/*` ref whose pull request MERGED -- by a same-named PR, or by the ref being the branch of a roster group the roster records `done` (`--roster-file`, via `roster_lib`);\n- enumerate the residue (no PR at all, or a closed-unmerged one) for an individual disposition; by default the owner's 2026-10-14 ruling archives then deletes it.\n\nThe archive arm runs FIRST: every ref it deletes is retagged at its own commit under `refs/tags/archive/<name>` before any deletion, and `--archive-scope none` deletes nothing -- so no tip is ever dropped unarchived. The plan is ordered (tags before deletes) and asserted in the self-test. The hazards are guards, not comments: a plan that would act on `main` raises; a `verdict/*` deletion is refused unless `--verdicts-drained` (the bus watcher reads those refs).\n\n`--dry-run` is the default and prints the plan; `--refs-file` / `--prs-file` reproduce a plan offline.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/prune_refs.py --self-test` -> SELF-TEST PASS (22 checks)\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` -> STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nThe self-test's own arms are the proof. Removing the open-PR keep rule reddens the null-control arm (\"open PR keeps even when merged\"); removing the merged-into-main rule reddens its arm; dropping the planner's guard reddens \"refuses a plan that would act on main\"; un-gating the verdict arm reddens \"refuses an undrained verdict ref\"; and moving any delete ahead of its tag reddens \"planner tags before deletes\".\n\n## Null control\n\nThe open-PR null control: a ref that satisfies BOTH the open-PR keep and the merged-into-main delete is KEPT -- proving the open-PR arm dominates rather than merely co-existing with the delete.\n\n## Red checks\n\nnone: no check went red on this branch; the new instrument adds no production code.\n\n## Architecture score\n\nn/a: no production code changed (`custom_components/` untouched), so the required `arch-score` check has no rise to explain.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\n`dev/governance/roles/fixer.md` -- the step-5 residue report and the archive/delete command list are this instrument's output, run by the orchestrator as account actions after the step-1/step-2 pull request merges.\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n","created_at":"2026-10-14T08:19:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T08:38:35Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T08:38:32Z","merged_at":"2026-10-14T08:38:32Z","merge_commit_sha":"30fda6ce1bc562d983a1b5212428b55b693b6bab","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2194/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2194/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2194/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/62bd768af874fb3750eff21b2fd49e3dad31dec1","head":{"label":"tvofi:closure/r9-prune-instrument","ref":"closure/r9-prune-instrument","sha":"62bd768af874fb3750eff21b2fd49e3dad31dec1","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gist